			"id": "Flows",
			"route": "/flows",
			"type": "index",
			"title": "Flows",
			"config": { "entitySource": "flows", "app": "buildiq" },
			"_note": "A flow is app-specific - a buildiq flow operates on buildiq's objects - so the authoring surface lives here rather than behind a deep link to OpenRegister's list. An ordinary index over the named `flows` source: a flow lives in the shared native flow store, not a register/schema pair, so the object-backed index had nothing to address until config.entitySource named the collection. Same store OpenRegister, integriq and hermiq use, so list and status semantics stay identical fleet-wide."
		},
